# OPTIONAL. You normally do NOT need this file — leave it unset and the app
# automatically talks to the API and WebSocket on the same address the page was
# opened from (correct whether you open it on the server or from another
# machine by the server's IP). Only set these if you serve the API from a
# DIFFERENT host than the frontend.
#
# Base URL of the Django backend API, served through the NGINX proxy:
# VITE_API_BASE=/api
# WebSocket base URL:
# VITE_WS_BASE=ws://YOUR_SERVER_IP/ws
